#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gpu-workload: hand the single 16 GB GPU between Strata (local LLM) and ComfyUI.

The two can't hold VRAM at the same time, so the GPU is in one of these modes:

  strata    Strata's model is loaded; ComfyUI holds no models and has no jobs.
  comfy     Strata's model is unloaded; ComfyUI may load models and run jobs.
  conflict  Strata is loaded while ComfyUI holds models or has jobs queued.

The mode is always derived from the live servers and nvidia-smi, never from a
state file, so `status` can't drift from reality and `switch` is idempotent:
switching to the mode you're already in only re-verifies it.

Commands:
  gpu-workload status [--json]
  gpu-workload switch strata|comfy [--wait SECONDS] [--json]
  gpu-workload check  strata|comfy [--json]
  gpu-workload hold comfy [--wait SECONDS] -- COMMAND...
  gpu-workload hook strata-before-load      (Strata's before_load; not for humans)

Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 failed / refused · 2 usage · 3 `check` found the wrong mode.
`hold` exits with COMMAND's own exit code once COMMAND has started.

The work is done by the vhotseat package in src/ (see src/vhotseat/compat.py).
"""

import sys
from pathlib import Path

# Installed as a symlink (~/.local/bin/gpu-workload): find src/ next to the real file.
sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent / "src"))

from vhotseat.compat import main  # noqa: E402

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
